This product bundles no third-party code and has no runtime dependencies. It
requires only Node.js (developed and tested on v24.12.0).

Adapted, not reimplemented
--------------------------
scripts/wmux-lanes.mjs is an ADAPTER over the `peer-sessions-wmux` helper
(`scripts/wmux_peer.py`), which is installed separately under the user's Codex
skills directory. That helper owns all wmux terminal control: spawning agents,
sending prompts, reading screens, stopping agents, and reaping exited surfaces,
including its fail-closed rules for unparseable control-plane output.

gaia-interagent deliberately does NOT duplicate that implementation. It shells
out to the helper and adds only bus identity, the lane limit, artifact-handoff
consumption, and a stale/exited sweep. It never passes `--yes` to the helper, so
it can never close a surface or stop an agent.

Derived work
------------
The bus core, event log, MCP server, and their test suite are derived from the
reviewed Gaia Claude/Codex interop prototype (Phase 3), whose 79 tests are ported
here unchanged apart from identifier renames.

Prior art acknowledged in the design
------------------------------------
- Anthropic's Claude Code cross-session messaging (`SendMessage`/`ListAgents`)
  informed the authority boundary. It is NOT used as a transport: it addresses
  Claude Code sessions only, on macOS/Linux, and cannot reach a non-Claude client.
- OpenAI's Codex MCP stdio server configuration informed the generated Codex
  adapter. No global Codex configuration is read or written by this product.
